sk was really to find  like-minded colleagues within the  organization  and we were very fortunate to be able to  partner our life sciences team  so they were a great advocate of  leveraging digital  in the work that they do whether it's in  terms of engaging customers and  our guests or in terms of leveraging  technology  in their work so i think with design  thinking it's given us a fantastic  framework  it gives us a common language and a  common goal to all work towards  are you all ready for the show all right  children come to the zoo and they say  i'm just going there to see animals  okay they come they go and then that's  it  one of the key things that we observed  was um that's the power of  being in the same exhibit as an animal  so a typical zoo always has a barrier  and i think when bodhiban we  conceptualize a space where the child  or the children are in the same space as  animals so you would have  the opportunity to be right next to a  rabbit or have a hedgehog in your hand  and i think that is the kind of emotion  that cannot be replicated  and so we started to try to understand  you know  amongst those families with kids what  were some of the  unmet needs that families and the  parents have  one was the need for more frequent  animal interactions but coming to the  zoo was just too troublesome  [Music]  by understanding all these key tensions  that parents have  we have actually conceptualized my  animal body  now their children can actually look at  our live camps  participate in virtual shows there are  so many  a variety of virtual activities that  they can enjoy  which makes our animal interaction a lot  more frequent  than it used to be this is my big  brother  pasha i like to annoy him when i'm bored  that's what siblings are for right all  right let me show you my really cool  friend  lastly is the accessibility to my number  buddy  that even a child in alaska right can  get to know  kansa our orangutan  for these we are really transforming how  families with children  experience the zoo what i've always  termed exporting mandai out of mundane  in order to reach you know consumers  outside of the confines  of our wildlife parks there is no  perfect situation  there is no perfect role there is no  perfect circumstance for us to drive  change and to drive innovation and we  make the best out of what we are given  [Music]  picture yourself now in the zoo and what  do you see  i hope like me you see endless  [Music]  possibilities  [Music]  you

